 "world": "⭐⭐⭐ E BASE RATE — R703's PREMISE IS REFUTED: F2's WEIGHT IS NOT OUR PARAMETERISATION. On the admissible population (all 42 arms, NOT the outcome-conditioned subset), the generator name is worth +0.000 to F2 under the canonical (family,k) partition — base rate 0.786, with the partition 0.786 — and its best gain over all 5 partitions is +0.048, i.e. 2 arms of 42, which no partition clears its own permutation null with. ⭐ SO THE ASYMMETRY R703 FOUND (20 unique exclusions against 4 and 2) IS A COUNT, NOT A SIGNAL: F2 excludes 33 of 42 arms, and a demanding clause produces many unique exclusions whatever it encodes. ⛔ AND BOTH OF MY OWN STATISTICS FAILED FIRST, EACH CAUGHT BY A CONTROL I REGISTERED: the cell-determined share was refuted by its SHAM (0.650 treatment vs 1.000 sham — under one cell every prediction counts as cell-determined), and the population was OUTCOME-CONDITIONED, which fixes the base rate at 1.000 for any clause excluding a majority and 0.000 for any clause excluding a minority, BY ALGEBRA and before any data. ⚠ F1 gains +0.048 at best and F3 +0.286, but F3's is a DERIVATION — F3 IS the predicate 1 < k <= 4, so a k-partition must recover it. ⚠ UNIT GAP: instrument unit is AN ARM, claim unit is A CLAUSE; at n=42 the resolution is 0.024 per arm, so a gain under 0.048 is two arms and the cross-clause ORDERING is reported while the cross-clause DIFFERENCE is not.",
